      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### What are Dataframes?\n",
        "Pandas has a very elegant way of managing data, very much borrowed from the statistical language R, mostly based around dataframes. You can think of dataframes a bit like an Excel table with rows, columns and common operations like sum, average and so on. We can use this on top of our previous work on lists and dictionaries (etc.) to make them more usable and malleable.\n",
        "\n",
        "To see how this works, we will build a small dataset by hand - in this case a [dictionary](https://github.com/MJMortensonWarwick/IB2AD0_Data_Science_GenerativeAI/blob/main/1_05_dictionaries.ipynb) holding the first four Titanic passengers."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "LsVLtmhH2WA1"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "passengers = {1:{'name':'Braund, Mr. Owen Harris', 'sex':'male', 'age':22.0, 'pclass':3, 'survived':0},\n",
        "              2:{'name':'Cumings, Mrs. John Bradley (Florence Briggs Thayer)', 'sex':'female', 'age':38.0, 'pclass':1, 'survived':1},\n",
        "              3:{'name':'Heikkinen, Miss. Laina', 'sex':'female', 'age':26.0, 'pclass':3, 'survived':1},\n",
        "              4:{'name':'Futrelle, Mrs. Jacques Heath (Lily May Peel)', 'sex':'female', 'age':35.0, 'pclass':1, 'survived':1}\n",
        "}\n",
        "passengers"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "BoZmysQo2p4Y"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "We can convert this to a Dataframe with great ease. Notice that each outer key (the passenger ID) becomes a column - adding `.T` (transpose) flips it so each passenger is a row, like in the full dataset:"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "W-szoAC42tIv"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "passengers_df = pd.DataFrame(passengers)\n",
        "passengers_df.T"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "7t8ATqP62xAl"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "We can even create such outputs from more complex dictionaries, such as a dictionary which includes a nested list. Here we group the first ten passengers by the port they embarked from (S = Southampton, C = Cherbourg, Q = Queenstown):"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "eeuSiBtn254W"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "ports = {'S':{'port':'Southampton', 'passengers':7, 'ids':[1, 3, 4, 5, 7, 8, 9]},\n",
        "         'C':{'port':'Cherbourg', 'passengers':2, 'ids':[2, 10]},\n",
        "         'Q':{'port':'Queenstown', 'passengers':1, 'ids':[6]}\n",
        "}\n",
        "ports"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "1k6GiP0N29XR"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "ports_df = pd.DataFrame(ports)\n",
        "ports_df"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "xcatviQm3DJM"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Pandas dataframes can also be built from various other data structures and sources (including Excel files, CSVs - as we did with `titanic.csv` - text files, databases and many more). For example, we can make our dataframe from a set of [lists](https://github.com/MJMortensonWarwick/IB2AD0_Data_Science_GenerativeAI/blob/main/1_04_lists.ipynb):"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "AebSOaD_3FJN"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "a = [22.0, 38.0, 26.0, 35.0]                    # age\n",
        "b = [\"male\", \"female\", \"female\", \"female\"]      # sex\n",
        "c = [False, True, True, True]                   # survived\n",
        "\n",
        "listdf = pd.DataFrame([a, b, c])\n",
        "listdf"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "ieLiBLDJ3H83"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
